<section class="block" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="overline">FAQ</div>
      <h2>What teams ask about Smarty vs <span class="grad-text">ioNova ARS</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq reveal">
      <div class="faq-item open">
        <button class="faq-q">Are Smarty and ioNova ARS actually competitors?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>No &mdash; they were built for different problems. Smarty is a postal verification API optimised for e-commerce checkout, shipping and CRM data quality. ioNova ARS is a SWIFT / ISO 20022 financial-messaging compliance engine and application. The sensible architecture retains Smarty for its lanes and routes payment traffic through ARS.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q">Can&rsquo;t we extend Smarty into SWIFT / ISO 20022 ourselves?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>The analysis is blunt: &ldquo;the architectural fit gap will not close with configuration or with a wrapper layer of reasonable size&rdquo;. The custom build &mdash; identifier pre-processor, ISO 20022 conversion, audit trail, sanctions adapter &mdash; totals 26&ndash;40 weeks versus weeks for ARS. As the analysis puts it, the difference is &ldquo;counted in calendar quarters, not basis points&rdquo;.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q">Smarty is sub-30ms &mdash; isn&rsquo;t speed what matters?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Speed is not scope. A sub-30ms postal answer still arrives without preserved financial identifiers, without corrected ISO 20022 XML and without a regulator-citable audit trail &mdash; so every fast response still needs the payments layer built around it. On raw performance the two tie; on what the response contains, they do not.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q">Is Smarty deterministic enough for payment audit?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>With a caveat. Smarty&rsquo;s reference-data updates can change output for identical input, and there is no customer-controlled version pinning &mdash; a reproducibility risk when an examiner asks why a payment parsed differently in March than in May. ioNova ARS output is bit-identical on versioned rule sets, so every historical decision can be replayed exactly.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q">Can we run Smarty and ioNova together?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Yes &mdash; and that is the recommended architecture. Run ioNova ARS as the parser of record in the payments pipeline, and keep Smarty downstream for postal enrichment, geocoding and the non-payment lanes &mdash; checkout, shipping and CRM &mdash; where it excels. The two roles do not overlap.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q">Does ioNova actually ship a UI, or is it another API?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
